  "notes": "Release date printed on page: 2026.2.12; HuggingFace MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.5 createdAt 2026-02-12T06:05:24Z agrees. JS-rendered news post (headless browser extraction); all benchmark scores are prose claims - coding/search charts exist as images without machine-readable values, rows are prose-verified where numbers are printed. RL scale disclosed: 200,000+ real-world environments, 10+ programming languages, full-lifecycle coverage (0-to-1 design through 90-to-100 review). Forge agent-native RL framework: tree-structured sample merging, ~40x training speedup; CISPO algorithm retained for MoE stability; process reward for long-context credit assignment. Efficiency economics (SWE-Bench Verified): 3.52M tokens/task avg (M2.1: 3.72M), end-to-end runtime 22.8 min (M2.1: 31.3; Opus 4.6: 22.9), 37% faster, cost per task 10% of Opus 4.6. Pricing: M2.5-Lightning 100 TPS at $0.3/M input + $2.4/M output; M2.5 50 TPS at half that; 'four instances running a year for $10,000'. Agentic round efficiency: ~20% fewer rounds than M2.1 across BrowseComp/Wide Search/RISE. VIBE benchmark upgraded to Pro version by the vendor (complexity/domain/accuracy increased)."
